  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you discard Loxodon Smiter and put it onto the battlefield, you've still discarded a card. Abilities that trigger when you discard a card (such as the one from Liliana's Caress) will still trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "18ac2282-83af-4acc-b20b-6a95771da688",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Domain abilities count the number of basic land types among lands you control, not how many lands you control or how many of any type.",
      "oracle_id": "1ba36042-8902-4abb-a4ae-a8d26d81a0de",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The basic land types are Plains, Island, Swamp, Mountain, and Forest. Land types other than basic land types (such as Desert) don't contribute to domain abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "1ba36042-8902-4abb-a4ae-a8d26d81a0de",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Cruel Celebrant dies at the same time as one or more other creatures and/or planeswalkers you control, its ability triggers for each of them.",
      "oracle_id": "3ee78cfc-0e9e-4737-a7e2-b42f94228040",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a planeswalker that's also a creature dies, Cruel Celebrant's ability triggers only once.",
      "oracle_id": "3ee78cfc-0e9e-4737-a7e2-b42f94228040",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a Two-Headed Giant game, Cruel Celebrant's ability causes the opposing team to lose 2 life and you gain 1 life.",
      "oracle_id": "3ee78cfc-0e9e-4737-a7e2-b42f94228040",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The size of the bonus is determined only as Tromp the Domains resolves. Once that happens, the bonus won't change later in the turn even if the number of basic land types among lands you control changes.",
      "oracle_id": "5b5dece6-b1e0-4844-bbf9-3b44008ffa70",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tromp the Domains affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won't gain trample or get a power and toughness boost.",
      "oracle_id": "5b5dece6-b1e0-4844-bbf9-3b44008ffa70",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Domain abilities count the number of basic land types among lands you control, not how many lands you control or how many of any type.",
      "oracle_id": "5b5dece6-b1e0-4844-bbf9-3b44008ffa70",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The basic land types are Plains, Island, Swamp, Mountain, and Forest. Land types other than basic land types (such as Desert) don't contribute to domain abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "5b5dece6-b1e0-4844-bbf9-3b44008ffa70",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The effect is based on the number of Swamps you control when Mutilate resolves. Only creatures on the battlefield at that time will be affected. The effect won't change later in the turn, even if the number of Swamps you control changes.",
      "oracle_id": "698e79ec-c2bc-4973-a095-f3c57b50e39c",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Count the number of lore counters on Scroll of the Masters as the activated ability resolves to determine how big a bonus the target creature gets. If Scroll of the Masters isn\u2019t on the battlefield at that time, use the number of lore counters on it when it left the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c7adde-492b-4585-8385-42d7e0d6e914",
      "published_at": "2014-11-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the activated ability has resolved, changing the number of lore counters on Scroll of the Masters won\u2019t affect the bonus that activation granted.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c7adde-492b-4585-8385-42d7e0d6e914",
      "published_at": "2014-11-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
